  "diagnosis": [
    "Every game starts with both outposts destroyed by the opposing aerial systems at about 7 s. The destroyed positions become temporary for their owners and then flip to the other team at about 12 s if the owner is absent, so the opening outpost state is a swap, not a stable hold.",
    "The base control point is independent of that fight. A base position is active while any robot occupies either its base card or its fortress card; the base card awards the position to a team that stays on it for five seconds. Controlling both base positions pays +3 control per second, three times the outpost rate.",
    "The baseline and both GPT styles send their sentry to the central-highland card and their infantry to the outposts; none of them guards the far side of its own base card. In the saved traces the sentry anchor sits at (27.1, 7.5) with 350 HP for the rest of the match and is never targeted.",
    "One robot on one home card is enough to keep that outpost position active. The two infantry therefore deny the opponent the +1/s outpost rate while the anchor accumulates +3/s. The home guards also body-block the ramp and keep the opponent off the central card.",
    "The anchor is the single point of failure. A death revives the robot but the 2027 engine also marks instant revives weak, so the anchor must return to its own supply zone to clear weakness before it can capture again. The pair version keeps a second body on the card during that window; the heavy version trades arrival speed for the largest health pool and keeps the sentry at home."
  ],
